                <pb facs="1099" n="949" sameAs="frus:frus1907p2/pg949"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 3714/1.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Persian Minister.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-01-09"><hi rendition="#italic">January 9,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: In acknowledging your note of this
                    date, I desire to express to you the profound sympathy of this Government for
                    the sorrow into which your country is plunged by the regretted death of His
                    Majesty Mozaffer-ed-Dine Shah. The President has to-day addressed a telegram to
                    His Majesty Mohammed Ali Shah tendering his sincere condolence for his
                    bereavement and that of the Persian nation.</p>
                <p>On this sorrowful occasion I beg to renew to you, Mr. Minister, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Elihu Root.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
